WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Take a sheet of glass and draw
one fine scratch across it.

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.820
Now bend it, with the
scratched side stretched.

3
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.920
It snaps cleanly, right along the line.

4
00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:14.100
Scratch a copper sheet
the same way and bend it.

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.420
It just bends.

6
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.880
Same scratch, same bend.

7
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.550
Why does one break and not the other?

8
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.140
In this mission, you'll sort
solids into three kinds:

9
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.360
crystalline, amorphous and polymeric.

10
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:31.280
Then you'll see how engineers
make glass and concrete stronger,

11
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:34.120
by putting their surfaces
under compression.

12
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: explain why the scratch
snaps the glass but not the copper.
